# nautobot-ansible-workshop-guide — attendee-facing lab guide.
#
# This repository is bound for public release: attendees are given it, and it
# is read as Network to Code's work product. Everything below is either noise
# that would look careless in a public repo, or something that must never
# reach one at all.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- OS / editor
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --------------------------------------------------------- AI / session files
# Deliberate, and a rule rather than a preference: CLAUDE.md, .claude/ and the
# session artifacts live ONE LEVEL UP, in the container directory that holds
# all three workshop repos. They describe how the workshop is *built* — which
# is confusing at best in a public repo, and is also the only way a single
# file can keep the cross-repo rules consistent. Ignored here so the rule
# cannot be broken by accident.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
nimbalyst-local/
*.plan.md

# --------------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
# Nothing in this repo should ever hold a credential — the workshop's static
# `admin`/`admin` literals are deliberate and documented, and everything else
# belongs in nautobot-ansible-workshop-instructor. These patterns are a
# backstop, not a licence to add one.
.env
.env.*
*.token
*.pem
*.key
secrets.yml
